Dicranum is a genus of mosses, also called wind-blown mosses or fork mosses. 
These mosses form in densely packed clumps. {{clarify|date=April 2023|reason=What is the difference between forking and branching?|text=Stems may fork, but do not branch.}} In general, upright stems will be single but packed together. Dicranum is distributed globally. In North America these are commonly found in Jack pine or Red pine stands.

